WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome back to "The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.100
It is time to play a game that tests

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.601
just how connected two people are to each other.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.534
It's time to play "Jinx"!

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:12.133
-♪ J-J-J-Jinx, J-J-J-Jinx ♪

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:15.234
-Our first team tonight, they're the Emmy-nominated founders

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.567
of Magnolia Network who've released

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.000
seven "New York Times" best-selling books.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.067
It is Chip and Joanna Gaines!

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.334
Come on!

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.334
-What?! What?!

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.167
-Yes. Welcome! Welcome, welcome!

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.534
Their opponents, they're the hosts

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:33.000
of the popular YouTube series "Good Mythical Morning,"

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.934
which is in its 23rd season.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.868
Give it up for Rhett and Link, ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:40.400
-Ohh. -Wow.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.868
Wow. -Boo!

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.868
-No, they can hear you. -Boo!

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.334
-Your microphone is on. Your mic --

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.901
-Boo! -The rules are very simple.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.534
-That's not a good look. That's not a good look.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.434
-I will give you a category.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.167
I don't even know why we mic'ed you.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.968
-Boo! -Stop.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.934
-I'm gonna give you a category, then you both count to "three"

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.801
and name something in that category at the same time.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:05.367
If you match, that's a jinx and you get a point.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.567
If you don't, the other team gets a chance to steal.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.801
Both teams, please put on your jinx gloves.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:10.901
-Okay. -Right.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.801
-This will help link your minds together.

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:13.901
-Oh. -We got it.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.067
-You got it. -We got it.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.234
-Yeah, so the gloves are connected.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.801
If you try to pull away... you can't.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.968
No. You are connected. -I think we're doing...

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.267
-Alright, once linked, feel free

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.234
to rest your arms on the provided elbow duvet.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.601
-Oh. -Oh, thank you for that.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.133
-This makes it easier.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.634
-I'm starting to shake a little. -Yeah, I don't want --

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.968
This is not an endurance game.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.501
This is more of a fun mental challenge.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.234
Chip and Joanna, you are up first.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.100
Can I have the category, please?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.200
-Oh, my gosh. That's amazing!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.534
-Right from the bank vault. -Your category --

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.968
Whew. Your category is...

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.501
power tools.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:49.968
-Oh. -Okay.

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.534
-Chip and Joanna -- I mean, this is --

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.734
-Alright. -You should know.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.000
-Okay. -Come on. We got this.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.234
-You got to say the same one.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.300
Chip and Joanna, whenever you're ready.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.801
-Got it. -One...

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:58.868
-You got it. -...two, three.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.300
-Drill! -Drill!

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.634
[ Bell dinging ] -Yes, you both said "drill."

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.000
-What did you say? -Drill!

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.701
-You said it. That's it. That's it.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.300
Drill. That is a jinx.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.434
You get a point and a lot of confetti.

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.868
Rhett and Link, you get to start this round.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.734
Here we go. Let's get your category, please.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.000
[ Air rushes ]

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:21.434
Ready? Category is... ice cream flavors.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.367
-Okay. -Ice cream flavors.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:24.868
You're -- You want the jinx.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.300
You guys are -- You're in the vibe.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.334
I can see you guys looking into each other's souls.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.567
-Oh, my gosh. -Look at -- Look at this.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.234
This is intense. -They're better than I thought.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.567
-Alright. Three, two, one.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.267
-Rainbow sherbet. -Chocolate-chip cookie dough.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:38.033
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:41.133
-Rainbow sherbet. -I couldn't -- Rainbow sherbet.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.934
-Come on, man. Everybody knows rainbow sherbet

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.601
is the first thing you think of. -That's true.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.501
-Chocolate-chip cookie dough is pretty good, too.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.000
Alright. Wow. You have a chance to steal.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.300
-Oh, we got this. We got this.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.434
-You got this? -This is easy.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.100
-Easy? Ooh, alright. Here we go.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.467
One, two, three.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:55.767
-Vanilla! -Vanilla!

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.434
-What?! [ Bell dinging ]

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:59.067
-Let's go. Let's go. -You love vanilla?

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:00.667
That's your thing? -That's our spot.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.133
-No, but I thought that's what he would pick.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.567
-You knew that that's what he would pick.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.501
-Well, it's peanut-butter chocolate, but it's so long,

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.033
so I just went straight for vanilla.

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:08.434
-I'm chocolate-chip cookie dough.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.968
-Rainbow sherbet. Okay. Here we go.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:12.767
Chip and Joanna, you're in the lead.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.400
You're kind of crushing right now, 2-zip.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.834
It is time for the next round. Can I get the category, please?

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:17.968
[ Air rushes ]

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.601
Words that start with "M."

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.601
-Ohh! -One, two, three.

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.701
-Magnolia! -Mom!

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:28.801
-Oh...

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:30.100
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.634
-Ohh! Your own company! -Dadgumit!

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:35.367
-You're all about the -- Well, you're all about the cash.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:38.501
Come on. Mom! Of course. -I'm a mom, you know.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:39.734
-Every time we say "Magnolia,"

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.734
they give us a $100 cashier's check.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.267
-You can't -- So, you can't say "Mom" or "magnolia."

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.300
-Dadgumit. -But you have a chance to steal.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.067
Word that starts with an "M." Get in there.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:52.367
Oh, my gosh. I can feel it! One, two, three.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.868
-Muskrat! -Mammal!

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.834
[ Buzzer ] -Oh! A muskrat is a mammal!

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.367
-No, no, no, no. -A muskrat is a mammal!

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.434
-No, I understand, but no. -Give us half a point!

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:01.968
-They nurse their young!

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.400
-Alright. Words that start with "M."

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.467
-Okay. Great. -One, two, three.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:07.567
-Mammogram. -Money.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.400
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.534
-No. -Hey.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.133
-Ahh. Unfortunately... -Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:17.767
-That's what I was thinking, Chip.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.267
[ Rasta horn blares ] -Ohh!

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.901
-You know what that sound means? -What?

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:23.133
-It means it's time for the final round.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.834
The first -- [ Laughter ]

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:27.868
The first team to jinx gets 10 points

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.634
and will be declared "Jinx" champions.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:30.767
-Oh! Oh! -Alright.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.667
-So it's anybody's game. -It's anyone's game.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.901
But, Chip and Joanna, you're up first.

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.501
-Let's go. -You get one chance to jinx.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:39.100
Otherwise, Rhett and Link can steal and take the whole game.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.300
-And we will.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.334
-Can we have the category, please?

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:43.267
[ Air rushes ]

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:45.667
[ Bell ding ]

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.067
-Well done. Well done.

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.300
-For 10 points.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.000
-Whew. Come on, babe.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.968
-Valentine's Day gifts.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:54.200
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.067
Valentine's Day gifts.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:58.267
-Okay. -One, two, three.

00:04:58.267 --> 00:04:59.567
-Jewelry. -Vacuum.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.667
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.701
-You -- They win it. You deserve to win.

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:07.033
-Alright. So, wait. -They don't even need to do it.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.968
-They want us to win so bad. -Jewelry or a vacuum.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.434
-He said a vacuum.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.400
-A vacuum. You could never give that.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.267
That is the worst Valentine's Day gift

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.901
in your entire lifetime.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.434
You guys got this. For the win. -We got it.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:21.567
-Valentine's Day gift. One, two, three.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:22.901
-Pony! -Pony!

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.000
-What?!

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.367
[ Bell dinging ]

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.968
-Yes!

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.934
-No way! -Oh, my God.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.367
-Well done.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:34.968
-Congratulations, Rhett and Link!

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.100
You have found the perfect link.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.267
And the fact you had it on Valentine's Day, of course,

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.000
it makes it much sweeter. Congratulations.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.801
Thanks to Chip and Joanna Gaines.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.067
Rhett and Link!

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.133
We're talking to Chip and Joanna after the break.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.634
Stick around, everybody. Come on back.

